  *ABE Guideline:* Explain briefly the objective, the problem statement, the method(s) you will use, and the relevance of the subject. Keep this to a maximum of half a page.

  *Example from ABE template:* "This project will investigate the detection of rotting in onions using spectral imaging immediately after harvest. The aim is to provide tools to facilitate early detection and removal of rotten onions, preventing post-harvest losses due to rot spread."

  *Tips:* Think of this as the elevator pitch for your entire thesis. A reader should walk away knowing: (1) what problem you are solving, (2) for whom, (3) how, and (4) why it matters. Write this section last — once the rest of the proposal is solid, distilling it into half a page becomes much easier.
