With Colombia consolidating as the global leader on Uchuva production with +90% of the shares of the market @noauthor_cundinamarca_2025. And as a high price export crop that has high family labor @ana_priscila_paez_parra_buenas_2012, there is a opportunity for the country to bring work and income to many more families that has to be exploited to replicate similar effects the coffee had on providing labor and welfare to the farmers. To do so several challenges need to be address at the same time.

One of these challenges is the target of this project -- the rotting in uchuvas (Physalis peruviana) due to Phoma and Botrytis--. The approach of this study will be to based interviews with the exporting companies, conversations with the comitee of exports of uchuva, videos, shared data, and problem statements get a clear view of the situation and the root causes from which a solution or set of solutions can be suggested.

The final aim of this project is to help the improvement of the shelf live of the crop, and lay the ground for more solid market growth.